# Memory accounting report

The memory manager tracks each process's declared pages against a global budget (default 512 MiB on the lab machine).

| Process | Declared | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| ai.embed | ~100 MiB | ONNX runtime linear memory; evicted by terminating the worker |
| ai.search | 1.5 MiB per vector segment | segments paged in from IndexedDB on demand |
| wm | 24 MiB | window snapshots for the overview |
| Terminal | 6–40 MiB | scrollback ring buffer + glyph atlas |

Over-budget events in the stress test (2× budget workload): accounted memory went over for at most 0.7 s before eviction brought it back. Evicted first: Exposé snapshots, then idle vector segments, then the embedding model.

Calibration: declared bytes were within 18 % of Chrome's own measurement.
